From 54ed3fe799ea27dec6e3a2693bac31b0021a2c53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:25:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(sim): judge and draw a necked tool at its drawn neck

The stack laws (reach c/c3, fixture c2/d2, posed and mesh sweeps, the
solid law's atoms) and the simulated tool read a tool's drawn cutter
outline over the shank span where it is narrower than the stated shank,
never wider - one source for the judged envelope, riding the existing
HolderStack seam as a `neck` field (`HolderStack::shank_bands`) and the
sim Cutter as `NeckBands`. No drawn cutter, one that no longer agrees
with the numbers, or one with no neck judges and draws bit-identically.
A drawn neck now enters the op stamp. Drill reach, the probe stylus and
multi-axis avoidance stay on the cylinder (#842).

Fixes #852

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
